@node "Introduction" "LDG CPX : Introduction"
@{B}Introduction@{b}
@Line 1 70 0 0 7

This CPX configures the LDG cookie ('LDGM'). In addition,
it can returns information about a library and about other 
LDG aspects.

This last version is specially designed for LDG 2 but it can 
work with LDG 1.xx system. However, a LDG 1.10 system is 
absolutly needed by the CPX.

The CPX is divided in four formulars, each formular can
be acces using the popup menu placed in the left down
corner of the CPX :

	Configure	F1	-> devoted to the LDG cookie configuration
	Library		F2  -> returns info on a library
	Expert		F3  -> performs expert commands and set some
					   special variables
	Information F4  -> General information


@endnode

@node "Configure menu" "LDG CPX : Configure menu"
@{B}Configure menu@{b}
@Line 1 70 0 0 7

You can access this menu by pressing the F1 key.
This formular returns information on your LDG configuration
and sets some important value such as :
	the path libraries : the path where *.LDG files are stored
	the garbage collector time : time between two garbage collector
								 performed by the LDG garbage deamon
								 (LDGD.APP) if LDG 2.xx is used
								 or by LDG manager if LDG 1.xx is
								 used.

In addition, the formular returns the 'LDGM' cookie version.


@endnode

@node "Library menu" "LDG CPX : Library menu"
@{B}Library menu@{b}
@Line 1 70 0 0 7
	
You can access this menu by pressing the F2 key.
This menu displays information about a LDG library. Select
a library to load with the F6 key. Informations retuned
are :
	- library version
	- LDG protocol version used (currently 1.00, 1.10, 1.20 or 2.00)
	- special flags of the library :
		* shared : the library may be shared with severals
				   clients. If a library is not shareable. A copy
				   of it is used.
		* resident : the library stays resident in memory after
					 loading.
		* locked : the library is locked : one and only one
				   client can used the library.
	- close function : the library has a closure function.
	- private extension : the library uses its own extension
	- special extension : if this is field is used, it indicated
		the library use a newer version of LDG protocol than
		recognize by the CPX : you should update your LDG system.

@endnode

@node "Expert menu" "LDG CPX : Expert menu"
@{B}Expert menu@{b}
@Line 1 70 0 0 7

You can access this menu by pressing the F3 key. This menu
is divided in two parts. The first part is devoted to send 
request to internal LDG kernel. For LDG 2.xx, LDG kernel is
included in the TSR LDG (AUTO\LDG.PRG) and you must select as
target item 'Tsr' in left popup. For LDG 1.xx, LDG kernel
is included in the LDG-manager (LDGMGR.APP) and have to 
select as target item 'Manager' in left popup. This popup
can be accessed by pressing F7 button.

Notice that we provide in LDG 2.10 package a new version
of manager which uses directly TSR functions. If a
client compatible LDG 1 uses this manager, libraries are
in fact shared with clients compatible LDG 2 (which was
not the case with older version of manager). In this case,
choice TSR or Manager as target is equivalent.

After choice the target, you can choice an action in the
right popup. This popup can be accessed by pressing F6
button. Possible actions are :
	- Garbage collector (F11): libraries unused will be unloaded
	- Reset (F12): all libraries will be discharged : be carefull !!
	- List loaded libs (F13): display in a popup the list of libraries
	                          loaded. You can select an item to display
	                           the list of client using the library.
	- Internal infos (F14): return information about capabilities of
	                        the system.
	- Shutdown (F15): this action is only possible with manager. It
				 	  send an AP_TERM message to the manager forcing
				      it to quit.

In addition, a field indicates the number of libraries currently
loaded.

The second part containt some variable used by LDG 1.xx but obsolete
with the new LDG version 2. The only setting is 'idle' which sets the
time idle (a value in millisecond unit). With LDG-manager 2.00 this
variable as no effect.

@endnode

@node "Information menu" "LDG CPX : Information menu"
@{B}Information menu@{b}
@Line 1 70 0 0 7

You can access this menu by pressing the F4 key. This menu
displays informations on LDG, Authors and Web access ...

@endnode

